{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useDebouncedCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/debouncer/useDebouncedCallback.ts#L42","children":[{"type":"text","value":"debouncer/useDebouncedCallback.ts:42"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A React hook that creates a debounced version of a callback function.\nThis hook is essentially a wrapper around the basic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"debounce"},{"type":"text","value":" function\nthat is exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/pacer"},{"type":"text","value":",\nbut optimized for React with reactive options and a stable function reference."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The debounced function will only execute after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince its last invocation. If called again before the wait time expires, the timer\nresets and starts waiting again."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This hook provides a simpler API compared to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useDebouncer"},{"type":"text","value":", making it ideal for basic\ndebouncing needs. However, it does not expose the underlying Debouncer instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For advanced usage requiring features like:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual cancellation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Access to execution counts"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom useCallback dependencies"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consider using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useDebouncer"},{"type":"text","value":" hook instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyFunction"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/ReactDebouncerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactDebouncerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", {\n}>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(..."},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"args"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Debounce a search handler\nconst handleSearch = useDebouncedCallback((query: string) => {\n  fetchSearchResults(query);\n}, {\n  wait: 500 // Wait 500ms between executions\n});\n\n// Use in an input\n<input\n  type=\"search\"\n  onChange={(e) => handleSearch(e.target.value)}\n/>","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useDebouncedCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [debouncer/useDebouncedCallback.ts:42](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/debouncer/useDebouncedCallback.ts#L42)\n\nA React hook that creates a debounced version of a callback function.\nThis hook is essentially a wrapper around the basic `debounce` function\nthat is exported from `@tanstack/pacer`,\nbut optimized for React with reactive options and a stable function reference.\n\nThe debounced function will only execute after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince its last invocation. If called again before the wait time expires, the timer\nresets and starts waiting again.\n\nThis hook provides a simpler API compared to `useDebouncer`, making it ideal for basic\ndebouncing needs. However, it does not expose the underlying Debouncer instance.\n\nFor advanced usage requiring features like:\n- Manual cancellation\n- Access to execution counts\n- Custom useCallback dependencies\n\nConsider using the `useDebouncer` hook instead.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyFunction`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`ReactDebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/ReactDebouncerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, \\{\n\\}\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(...`args`) => `void`\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Debounce a search handler\nconst handleSearch = useDebouncedCallback((query: string) => {\n  fetchSearchResults(query);\n}, {\n  wait: 500 // Wait 500ms between executions\n});\n\n// Use in an input\n<input\n  type=\"search\"\n  onChange={(e) => handleSearch(e.target.value)}\n/>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useDebouncedCallback\ntitle: useDebouncedCallback\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useDebouncedCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [debouncer/useDebouncedCallback.ts:42](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/debouncer/useDebouncedCallback.ts#L42)\n\nA React hook that creates a debounced version of a callback function.\nThis hook is essentially a wrapper around the basic `debounce` function\nthat is exported from `@tanstack/pacer`,\nbut optimized for React with reactive options and a stable function reference.\n\nThe debounced function will only execute after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince its last invocation. If called again before the wait time expires, the timer\nresets and starts waiting again.\n\nThis hook provides a simpler API compared to `useDebouncer`, making it ideal for basic\ndebouncing needs. However, it does not expose the underlying Debouncer instance.\n\nFor advanced usage requiring features like:\n- Manual cancellation\n- Access to execution counts\n- Custom useCallback dependencies\n\nConsider using the `useDebouncer` hook instead.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyFunction`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`ReactDebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/ReactDebouncerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, \\{\n\\}\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(...`args`) => `void`\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Debounce a search handler\nconst handleSearch = useDebouncedCallback((query: string) => {\n  fetchSearchResults(query);\n}, {\n  wait: 500 // Wait 500ms between executions\n});\n\n// Use in an input\n<input\n  type=\"search\"\n  onChange={(e) => handleSearch(e.target.value)}\n/>\n```\n"}
